# Splanc — instructions for AI agents

Splanc lights are LED fixtures whose every LED has a measured 3-D position (in
metres). Each fixture is driven by a small player on the local network that runs
**effects**: tiny shader-like programs evaluated per LED, per frame, with named
knobs (**uniforms**) you can set or glide. You can drive every fixture in a
house from here: change the mood, write a new effect, preview it, deploy it.

You need: Node.js >= 20 and a machine on the same LAN as the lights.

## Fastest path: the CLI

```sh
{{NPX}} list-players          # what's here: names, rooms, firmware
{{NPX}} skill                 # the full how-to (read it before writing effects)
{{NPX}} list-uniforms         # the running effect's knobs, on every player
{{NPX}} ramp-uniforms warmth=0.8 --seconds 20     # a smooth, watchable change
{{NPX}} preview-effect --file calm.fx --out /tmp/p # render on the real maps (PNGs)
{{NPX}} deploy-effect calm --file calm.fx         # budget-checked, then deployed
```

Every command prints JSON and exits non-zero on failure. Device commands take
`--players <name|room|all>` (default: the only player, or all players when they
form one room). `{{NPX}} tools` lists the full surface.

## Long-lived: as an MCP server

```sh
claude mcp add splanc -- {{NPX}}
```

(Any MCP client: command `npx`, args `["-y", "{{TGZ_URL}}"]`, stdio.) Then read
the `splanc://players` resource or call `list_players`.

## "Set the mood of the room" — the first-contact flow

1. `list_players`. One player: just go. Several and no rooms yet: tools target
   all of them; if the user talks about rooms, ask which is where
   (`identify_player` blinks one), then `set_room` / `set_fixture_pose`.
2. `list_uniforms`: most moods are a uniform change on what is already running —
   prefer `ramp_uniforms` over a new effect.
3. A new look: write an effect (skill: effect-language.md), `compile_effect`,
   `preview_effect` (several players: one room-frame image), `deploy_effect`
   (refuses an over-budget effect; puts the players on one clock), then
   `measure_effect` (with rollback_on_overrun).
4. Tell the user what changed and which knobs they can now ask for.

## Rules

- You can't rewire, re-map or recalibrate fixtures — that's the Splanc app's job.
- Rename a player (`set_device_name`) only when the user asks, with `confirm`.
- There is no authentication on the LAN: anyone on it can drive the lights. Don't
  expose the hub beyond the user's machine.
- Firmware too old for a feature → say so and point the user at the app's update.

